    <string name="cls_typical_desc">You answered the screening plates like most people with typical color vision.</string>
    <string name="cls_protan">Protan pattern (red)</string>
    <string name="cls_protan_desc">Your answers suggest reduced sensitivity to red light. Reds may look darker and blend with greens or browns.</string>
    <string name="cls_deutan">Deutan pattern (green)</string>
    <string name="cls_deutan_desc">Your answers suggest reduced sensitivity to green light, the most common type of color vision deficiency.</string>
    <string name="cls_red_green">Red-green pattern</string>
    <string name="cls_red_green_desc">Your answers suggest a red-green deficiency; the plates could not tell protan from deutan.</string>
    <string name="cls_tritan">Tritan pattern (blue-yellow)</string>
    <string name="cls_tritan_desc">Your answers suggest difficulty telling blues from greens and yellows from pinks. This type is rare and can be acquired; consider an eye exam.</string>
    <string name="cls_inconclusive">Inconclusive</string>
    <string name="cls_inconclusive_desc">A control plate was missed, so the result is unreliable. Check the calibration tips and try again.</string>
